* text=auto eol=lf

# The recordings of the old tools are evidence, not text this repository owns:
# no line-ending normalisation, so a case stays byte for byte what was recorded.
testdata/cases/1a-source/** -text

# The rendered package is evidence of the Python format, not text this
# repository owns: the D3 segment carries a lone carriage return on purpose.
internal/brain/maintenance/testdata/package.golden.md -text

# The stamp cache is evidence of the Python format: `_write_stats` produced
# these bytes, and a fold of any kind would make the comparison a comparison
# with this repository rather than with the reference.
internal/brain/maintenance/testdata/stats.golden.tsv -text

# The diff goldens are evidence of `difflib`'s answers, not text this
# repository owns: the test holds them byte for byte against what `_hunks`
# wrote, and a fold of any kind would make the comparison a comparison with
# this repository rather than with the reference. Neither file holds a raw
# carriage return today -- JSON escapes the one a hand vector carries -- so
# the attribute guards a byte-exact record, not a byte a fold would break now.
internal/brain/maintenance/testdata/hunks.golden.json -text
internal/brain/maintenance/testdata/hunks-fuzz.golden.json -text

# The package and the case file are evidence of the Python format for the same
# reason `package.golden.md` above is: `_segments`, `render_package` and
# `write_case` produced these bytes.
internal/brain/maintenance/testdata/case-package.golden.md -text
internal/brain/maintenance/testdata/case.golden.toml -text

# The merge package and the merge case file are the same kind of evidence:
# `_merge_evidence` over a real repository, `render_package` and `write_case`
# produced these bytes.
internal/brain/maintenance/testdata/merge-package.golden.md -text
internal/brain/maintenance/testdata/merge-case.golden.toml -text

# The bundle frame is evidence of `init_bundle`'s bytes: an oracle over
# src/brain/wiki/scaffold.py wrote these files, and a fold of any kind would
# make the comparison a comparison with this repository rather than with the
# reference.
internal/brain/wiki/testdata/bundle/*.golden -text

# The stage-3a recordings and their translation compare whole file worlds byte
# for byte -- stat caches, registers, case files, the bytes `brain init` wrote.
# A fold of any kind would compare with this repository, not with the reference.
testdata/cases/3a-source/** -text
testdata/cases/3a/** -text
